elena Foulkes enters the general as a clear favorite over Republican Aaron Guckian. Every recent poll shows Foulkes ahead by 22 to 27 points, though a large share of voters remains undecided. All seven major race ratings call the contest Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets put the chance of a Democratic win near 97%.\n\nThe state's Democratic lean of about eight points gives Foulkes a structural edge, and Guckian has drawn negative coverage for skipping forums while seeking support in Florida. Independent Ken Block argues he could win if Guckian withdrew, but the Republican is staying in, splitting the change vote. The main uncertainty is the size of the margin, not the likely winner, with undecided voters and minor-party candidates still to be allocated.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.1}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.997, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9964, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9941, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9953, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9924, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 16.0}]}